    {
      "id": "claim_9d22dbd5fa1342079ec0dd72bec3ce29",
      "statement": "The physics vertical slice is the [v1] bounded, CLI-verifiable proof domain defined in ARCHITECTURE.md §8: a fact schema for kinematic/mechanical quantities with dimension/unit attributes, a manual rule library covering v=u+at, v^2=u^2+2as, s=ut+1/2 at^2, s=(u+v)/2 t, t=(v-u)/a, F=ma, K=1/2 mv^2 and W=Fs, multi-step composition, induction and deduction modes with deduction used for word problems, natural-language input, a sympy algebra hook, full verbose trace plus success-path/failure-trail/full renders, a 15+ problem benchmark gate, and first-class unknown handling.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://ARCHITECTURE.md#L318-L350",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ef23965d8b9b3f09fc374ec94e8f015cd5d30fe99fd19516774dff40c70ab4a6:"
        }
