      "id": "claim_95ceea86b4d04f6aa0917c575662af73",
      "statement": "The physics grammar is the [v1] manual-grammar slice: auto-extraction is [out-v1] and benchmark-gated — a candidate auto-extracted grammar passes the §5.2 gate only if it solves every must-solve case, rejects every must-reject case with unknown/no-solution (never a wrong number), produces fully traceable derivations, and demonstrably enforces its checks; a failing grammar is discarded or sent for revision, and manual authorship remains the deterministic fallback [v1].",
